@startuml 02f-deployment-local
title sphinx-asr deployment — single-machine (today, pre-integration)

skinparam defaultFontName Menlo

node "User workstation\n(Linux / macOS / WSL)" {

    artifact "sphinx-asr/\n(SPHINX_ROOT)" as Root {
        file "sphinx.sh\n(entrypoint)" as Entry
        file "Makefile" as Mk
        file "requirements.txt" as Reqs
        file ".venv/\n(auto-created on first run)" as Venv
        folder "scripts/\n(Python)" as Scripts
        folder "vendor/\n(C + Perl source)" as Vendor
        folder "bin/<arch>/\n(built binaries)" as Bin
        folder "corpus/<name>/" as Corpus
        folder "experiments/NNN/" as Exps
    }
}

artifact "OS-level tools" {
    file "python3" as Py
    file "perl" as Perl
    file "sox" as Sox
    file "make, gcc, cmake" as Toolchain
}

Entry --> Venv     : creates + pip install
Entry --> Scripts  : python3 scripts/<cmd>.py
Entry --> Bin      : PATH prepend bin/<arch>
Mk   --> Vendor    : cmake / make install\n→ bin/<arch>/
Mk   --> Toolchain : cc, cmake
Scripts --> Vendor : subprocess perl\nvendor/sphinxtrain/scripts/NN.*/slave_*.pl
Scripts --> Corpus : read corpus.yml, audio, dict, lm
Scripts --> Exps   : read/write experiment.yml,\netc/, model_parameters/,\nlogdir/, bwaccumdir/, result/
Bin     --> Py     : sphinx_fe, pocketsphinx_batch are\nC binaries, invoked as subprocesses
Scripts --> Py     : runs under .venv interpreter

note right of Exps
  **All state local.** Training's Baum-Welch
  accumulator passes, decoder partitions, and
  logs all live on the same filesystem as the
  Python / Perl / C processes that produce them.

  No Slurm, no NFS, no cross-host anything.
end note

note right of Root
  Parallelism limited to:
  - feats.py ThreadPoolExecutor across local cores
  - Queue::POSIX fork-pool inside slave_*.pl
    (capped by CFG_NPART, default 1)
end note

@enduml
